  "body": "I'm wondering if there's any mileage in allowing indeterminate to be set using an actual attribute in HTML? i.e. being able to (statically) set a checkbox to be `<input type=\"checkbox\" indeterminate>`, to match the same way this can be done but only for assistive technologies with `<input type=\"checkbox\" aria-checked=\"mixed\">`? again, it feels odd that it's possible to express this semantic concept in markup, but only for AT.\r\n\r\n(split from https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/5079#issuecomment-813111427)",
